IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja3-sch6-sixth-schedule`

-- scja3-tests-sch6.l4: tests for the Sixth Schedule.  Expected values are written from the text of the Schedule
-- (SCJA1969.txt lines 6172-6263) beside each assertion, and not from the module's output.

§ `Tests: the Sixth Schedule`

GIVEN court IS A Court
      jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
      subject IS A `Subject of the case`
GIVETH A Decision
`sch 6 test: a decision` MEANS
    Decision WITH
        `made by` IS court
        `in the exercise of` IS jurisdiction
        `nature of the proceeding` IS nature
        `subject of the case` IS subject
        `the order` IS (Order OF `another order or application`, `made, being neither a grant nor a refusal`)
        `made after the trial of an action` IS FALSE
        `made by consent of the parties` IS FALSE
        `amount in dispute or value of the subject matter, excluding interest and costs` IS NOTHING
        `date made` IS Date 1 7 2024
        `date the judgment or order was extracted` IS NOTHING
        `a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies` IS FALSE
        `the parties agreed in writing, signed by or for each, that it is final` IS FALSE

GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of the case`
GIVETH A Decision
`sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` subject

`sch 6 test: constitutional law` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `constitutional or administrative law`
`sch 6 test: contempt` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `contempt of court`
`sch 6 test: arbitration` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` arbitration
`sch 6 test: international commercial arbitration` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `international commercial arbitration`
`sch 6 test: corporate insolvency` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `insolvency, restructuring or dissolution of a corporation, limited liability partnership or sub-fund of a variable capital company`
`sch 6 test: bankruptcy of an individual` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` bankruptcy
`sch 6 test: patents` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` patents
`sch 6 test: admiralty` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `admiralty or shipping`
`sch 6 test: Parliamentary elections` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `Parliamentary elections`
`sch 6 test: Presidential elections` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `Presidential elections`
`sch 6 test: Mediation Act 2017` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `recording a mediated settlement agreement under the Mediation Act 2017`
`sch 6 test: Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `an international settlement agreement under the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020`
`sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter` MEANS `sch 6 test: a General Division original civil decision on the subject` `any other civil matter`
`sch 6 test: SICC ordinary civil matter` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` `any other civil matter`
`sch 6 test: GD appellate civil decision on an ordinary matter` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` `any other civil matter`
`sch 6 test: GD supervisory decision` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `General Division` `supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` `any other civil matter`
`sch 6 test: GD criminal decision on a constitutional matter` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a criminal proceeding` `constitutional or administrative law`
`sch 6 test: FD decision` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `Family Division of the High Court` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` `any other civil matter`
`sch 6 test: AD decision` MEANS `sch 6 test: a decision` `Appellate Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` `constitutional or administrative law`

-- ---- the limbs, one by one ----
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(a) the appeal arises from a case relating to constitutional or administrative law` `sch 6 test: constitutional law`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(a) the appeal arises from a case relating to constitutional or administrative law` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(b) the appeal arises from a case relating to contempt of court` `sch 6 test: contempt`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(b) the appeal arises from a case relating to contempt of court` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(c) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of arbitration` `sch 6 test: arbitration`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(c) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of arbitration` `sch 6 test: international commercial arbitration`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(c) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of arbitration` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(d) the appeal arises from a case relating to the insolvency, restructuring or dissolution of a corporation, limited liability partnership or sub-fund` `sch 6 test: corporate insolvency`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the limb names a corporation, a limited liability partnership and a sub-fund; the bankruptcy of an individual is not among them
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(d) the appeal arises from a case relating to the insolvency, restructuring or dissolution of a corporation, limited liability partnership or sub-fund` `sch 6 test: bankruptcy of an individual`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(e) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of patents` `sch 6 test: patents`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(e) the appeal arises from a case relating to the law of patents` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(ea) the appeal arises from a case relating to admiralty law or shipping law` `sch 6 test: admiralty`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(ea) the appeal arises from a case relating to admiralty law or shipping law` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(f) the appeal is against a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `sch 6 test: SICC ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(f) the appeal is against a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(g) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Parliamentary Elections Act 1954` `sch 6 test: Parliamentary elections`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(g) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Parliamentary Elections Act 1954` `sch 6 test: Presidential elections`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(h) the appeal is against a judgment or order in an action under section 47(8) of the Presidential Elections Act 1991` `sch 6 test: Presidential elections`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(h) the appeal is against a judgment or order in an action under section 47(8) of the Presidential Elections Act 1991` `sch 6 test: Parliamentary elections`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (i): each of the eight provisions
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(i) section 32(1) of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(ii) section 21A(1), 45(7) or 49(11) of the Arbitration Act 2001`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(iii) section 74(4) of the Competition Act 2004`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(iv) section 10(4) of the International Arbitration Act 1994`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(v) section 18(5) of the Maintenance of Parents Act 1995`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(vi) section 90(3) of the Patents Act 1994`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(vii) section 35(4) of the Personal Data Protection Act 2012 as in force immediately before 1 February 2021, or section 48R(4) of that Act`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i)(viii) section 17(8), 29(9), 35(7) or 44(9) of the Protection from Online Falsehoods and Manipulation Act 2019`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(i) the appeal is made under one of the eight provisions named` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(j) the appeal is made under a written law that provides for the appeal to lie to the Court of Appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(j) the appeal is made under a written law that provides for the appeal to lie to the Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(k) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Mediation Act 2017` `sch 6 test: Mediation Act 2017`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(k) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Mediation Act 2017` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(l) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` `sch 6 test: Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 para 1(l) the appeal is against a decision or order under the Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` `sch 6 test: Mediation Act 2017`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---- the scope ----
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter`
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: GD appellate civil decision on an ordinary matter`
#ASSERT `sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: SICC ordinary civil matter`
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: GD supervisory decision`)
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: GD criminal decision on a constitutional matter`)
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: FD decision`)
#ASSERT NOT (`sch 6 para 1 the decision is within the Schedule's scope` `sch 6 test: AD decision`)

-- ---- seam 8: the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal ----
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: constitutional law` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: contempt` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: international commercial arbitration` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: corporate insolvency` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: patents` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: admiralty` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: SICC ordinary civil matter` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: Parliamentary elections` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: Presidential elections` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: Mediation Act 2017` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: Singapore Convention on Mediation Act 2020` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an ordinary civil matter, but the appeal is made under a named provision, or under another written law that says so
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter` `sch 6 para 1(i)(vi) section 90(3) of the Patents Act 1994` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an ordinary civil matter and no limb: the Schedule does not send it to the Court of Appeal
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: ordinary civil matter` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: bankruptcy of an individual` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: GD appellate civil decision on an ordinary matter` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- outside "the exercise of its original or appellate civil jurisdiction" or outside the General Division
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: GD supervisory decision` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: GD criminal decision on a constitutional matter` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: FD decision` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `sch 6 test: AD decision` `sch 6 para 1(i) none of those provisions` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`sch 6 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 6 the limbs taken together` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING)) EQUALS NOTHING
